One portable page script (toolkit/toolkit_core.js, no Meridian APIs: it can
ship as an MV3 extension later) plus Meridian's adapter (toolkit_meridian.js),
injected into an isolated world of the tab's main frame on DOMContentLoaded
when meridian.toolkit.enabled (or --enable-meridian-toolkit) is on.
ToolkitTabHelper polls the page's queue (60 ms while a tool is up, 400 ms
idle, only for a visible tab) and does what the page can't: the clipboard
(text, HTML, PNG), real pixels of the tab (CopyFromSurface, CSS px x zoom),
the toolkit's store (pref meridian.toolkit.store). The page menu gets four
items with the flag on (IDC_MERIDIAN_TOOLKIT_*), declared in :model
(toolkit_menu.h) so the menu needs no new GN dep. Synthetic events from the
page don't drive the toolkit (isTrusted).

